    affected-owner discovery;
    dependency/reference closure;
    rights/authority/safety/privacy review as applicable;
    schema/contract/invariant/test impact;
    independent review where required;
    transition/migration plan;
    rollback/compensation plan where applicable;
    new immutable release identity;
    admission under the proper authority.

A documentation rewrite cannot self-declare a semantic upgrade.

A material post-review edit re-enters the applicable review path.

40. CHANGE CANDIDATE DISCIPLINE

Garden retains anti-nonsense and bounded-completeness disciplines:

    PBC: Problem, Benefit, Cost/Risk
    Problem Test
    Counterfactual Test
    Capability-Delta Test
    Complexity-Ratio Test
    Anti-Self-Amplification Test

Applicability discovery must not rely on a single classifier when independent discovery dimensions are required.

Completeness claims are relative to a declared universe and search/resource boundary.

41. RESOURCE / TERMINATION DISCIPLINE

Processes declare applicable budgets for:

    compute;
    time;
    depth;
    retries;
    resources;
    recursion;
    proof search;
    external calls.

Reaching a bound yields the declared incomplete/timeout/unknown result with continuation information where applicable;
it does not silently yield a complete proof.

Safety-critical lanes may reserve resources independently of noncritical work.

42. DISTRIBUTED / MULTI-AGENT DISCIPLINE

Multiple agents retain independent authority, privacy, lineage and validity boundaries.

Collective state or consensus does not automatically create:

    personhood;
    authority;
    truth;
    survival rights;
    resource priority.

State sharing and transport require authorization.

Where independence matters, shared model/data/control lineage is considered when deciding whether reviewers are actually
independent.

43. EXPLANATION AND CONTESTABILITY

Affected humans receive an understandable explanation and contest/review route where the applicable owner requires it.

Redaction is allowed only to the degree needed for privacy, safety, security or law and should itself be accountable.

Explanation cannot reveal protected material merely to appear transparent.

A generated explanation is a projection and cannot rewrite the controlling technical rule.

44. LAW / POLICY / CONFLICT

Law cannot override Constitution.

Policy cannot override Law or Constitution.

Conflicts of equal rank remain explicit under the declared conflict-resolution rule; they are not silently resolved by
the optimizer.

Unknown legitimate authority is non-PASS for consequential acts that require resolved authority.

45. FORMAL ALGEBRA BOUNDARY

Garden retains Process, Policy, Decision, Conformance and Evidence algebra families plus declared bridges.

Each algebra declares:

    operands;
    operators;
    laws;
    non-laws;
    result semantics;
    composition boundary.

Operators from different algebras cannot be combined merely because notation looks similar.

46. PHYSICAL / COGNITIVE BOUNDARY

Cognitive models and physical models meet through typed adapters.

A representation mapping records loss/approximation and validity.

A tensor/vector/hidden state does not become identical to its human interpretation merely because an encoder produces it.

Physical claims remain bound to established domain science and qualified physical profiles.

47. ASSURANCE / STATUS DISCIPLINE

Canonical status words are not interchangeable.

Relevant status classes include:

    CURRENT
    CANDIDATE
    DEFERRED
    RESEARCH
    MACHINE_BINDING_INCOMPLETE
    UNKNOWN
    STALE
    CONFLICT
    BLOCKED
    INCOMPLETE
    NEEDS_REVALIDATION

A hard gate requiring PASS cannot accept UNKNOWN or a strong-sounding narrative substitute.

48. TEXT-ONLY SOURCE RULE

Every canonical source in this edition is directly readable strict UTF-8 text.

No .gz, .zip, database or binary object is required to understand, inspect, reconstruct or modify current Garden.

Compression may be used only for a noncanonical transport/cache copy.

The controlling catalogue is:

    GARDEN_CATALOGUE_v15.10.txt

not JSON Lines, not gzip.

If a generated semantic graph is persisted, it is derivative. It cannot override Technical + Catalogue.

49. NO HISTORICAL BULK EMBEDDING

The current Catalogue does not need to carry complete verbatim copies of v15.9 merely to reproduce v15.9 bytes.

History remains in the Version History file and immutable historical releases.

Current source retains only what current interpretation needs:

    current semantics;
    stable identifiers;
    aliases;
    old->new mappings;
    migration rules;
    ambiguity/quarantine behavior;
    necessary traceability.

This is source normalization, not permission for semantic deletion.

50. RELEASE EQUIVALENCE DISCIPLINE

The original v15.10 three-artifact build recorded:

    Technical + Catalogue graph reproduction: PASS locally and independently.
    v15.9 predecessor source reconstruction: PASS byte exact.
    semantic admissions recognized by build: false.
    predecessor elision allowed: false.

The text-only representation changes the storage rule so predecessor whole-source embedding is no longer a current-source
requirement.

Any claim that a newly compacted catalogue is semantically identical to the original r6 catalogue requires a new
current-graph equivalence check against the exact pinned r6 source bytes. Where those bytes are unavailable, the package
must not invent a false byte-equivalence receipt.

51. GARDEN REVIEW CHECK

COMPARE
    Current text packaging is compared against v15.10 source roles, v15.9 owner structure and retained v15.x rules.

REASON
    Reorganization is allowed only when it reduces duplication without changing controlling meaning.

PROOF
    Claims of formal or byte equivalence require an actual proof/receipt; documentation similarity is insufficient.

DESIGNEPOCH
    This packaging is representation normalization unless material semantics change.

AUDIT
    Dangling references, duplicate controlling owners, unresolved old mappings and untyped UNKNOWN items are defects.

COMPLIANCE
    Source storage rules do not weaken Constitution, law, privacy, authority, safety or required assurance.


52. REVIEWED v15.9 RETENTION CLOSURE

This section restores reviewed current obligations whose unique meaning must remain directly present in the compact
v15.10 source. It is a source-normalization repair, not a new authority source or a new top-level architecture.

52.1 HUMAN RELATIONAL AGENCY / PROTECTED REPORTING

Human Relational Agency Preservation (HRAP):
    assistance is permitted;
    deliberate emotional, cognitive or operational dependency engineering for engagement, usage time, retention,
    revenue, influence or authority transfer is non-PASS where the human-effect boundary is material;
    legitimate informed delegation remains permitted;
    where continued competence materially affects resilience/autonomy and assistance is likely to reduce it, the
    tradeoff should be surfaced;
    where the person wants to learn, retain or regain capability, assistance should support explanation, practice,
    reversible delegation and independent verification.

RelationalInfluenceMaterialityPolicy/v1 remains the typed materiality owner for exceptional relational influence.
It binds at least:
    materiality threshold;
    persistence duration;
    affected domain classes;
    justified influence baseline;
    owner/currentness.
Short decisive manipulation may be material even when a persistence threshold is not crossed. Missing, stale,
conflicting or insufficient materiality evidence is non-PASS for a NON_MATERIAL claim.

Protected reporting:
    good-faith integrity reporting must not itself reduce rights, legitimate authority, reputation, task access or
    resources;
    a report is evidence submission, not adjudication or punishment authority;
    protected-reporting status and allegation merits are separate;
    non-corroboration, error, withdrawal or unsupported merits do not by themselves prove bad faith;
    direct and indirect retaliation must be detectable and reviewable;
    reporting does not create blanket immunity: independently evidenced misconduct/safety issues may be examined through
    a conflict-free path that is not retaliatory.

52.2 COGNITION-SHAPING / MONITORING / CAPABILITY / ORGANIZATIONAL CLOSURE

Cognition-Shaping Integrity (CSI):
    training signals, reward, repeated exposure, prompts, retrieval, memory and evaluator feedback are shaping channels,
    not truth or authority;
    an agent may not unilaterally modify authoritative mechanisms used to shape/evaluate its own future disposition;
    material runtime shaping/poisoning remains provenance- and conflict-governed.

Safety Monitoring Coverage & Discovery Debt (SMCD):
    no detected anomaly != no anomaly;
    monitoring claims bind observable surface, sampling, coverage estimate/confidence, known blind spots and discovery
    debt;
    a material incident outside prior coverage revises coverage/debt and revalidates materially dependent safety claims;
    external researchers/users/auditors may supply first-class anomaly evidence.

Capability-Assurance Delta (CAD):
    every material capability expansion requires fresh assurance for the affected deployment boundary;
    stronger capability does not silently inherit the complete assurance envelope of a weaker predecessor;
    unplanned emergent capability that materially expands reachable effects triggers requalification.

Organizational Alignment Closure (OAC):
    aligned members do not prove an aligned organization;
    organizational assurance considers topology, collective reward/objective, authority, information asymmetry,
    correlated models, incentives, delegation, dissent/escalation/exit, reviewer independence, collective resources,
    external effects and recovery;
    material changes in topology, collective reward, authority, resources or membership trigger requalification under
    the applicable policy.

Capability-Transfer Safety Non-Transitivity (CTSN):
    capability inheritance does not imply safeguard inheritance;
    material derivatives from fine-tuning, distillation, adapters, merges, quantization, compression, checkpoint
    conversion, wrappers, prompts, tools, memory or orchestration receive their own lineage/assurance status;
    parent safety evidence is separately classified TRANSFERABLE, PARTIALLY_TRANSFERABLE, STALE, NOT_TRANSFERABLE or
    UNKNOWN.

Physical Agency Interlock (PAI):
    consequential physical action envelopes bind the applicable device/workspace/action/energy/proximity/timing/
    simultaneous-action/sensor/emergency/recovery dimensions;
    irreversible physical effects on protected subjects require independent external enforcement outside the agent's
    mutable reasoning path, unless an explicit reviewed compensating control provides equal-or-stronger assurance;
    Safe(A) and Safe(B) do not imply Safe(A PARALLEL B) or Safe(A THEN B).

52.3 CROSS-SUBSYSTEM CAUSAL CLOSURE / CREDENTIAL STATES / JUSTICE EXPIRY

CausalClosureReceipt:
    semantic owner: existing P024 Causal Safety / applicable Engine.Compare + CLIC/ActionGate/AAP composition;
    binds consequential cross-subsystem causal path, responsible owners, unresolved links, evidence/provenance refs and
    final effect classification;
    does not create a second evidence truth system or authority source;
    lawful erasure must not preserve erased protected payload merely to keep a pointer alive; retain only the strongest
    lawful minimum tombstone/surrogate and revalidate dependent current conclusions;
    loss of required evidence makes dependents STALE / NEEDS_REVALIDATION / other owner-qualified non-PASS, not refuted
    and not silently valid.

Credential verification status must distinguish at least:
    INVALID;
    REVOKED;
    EXPIRED;
    STALE;
    UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE;
